 "consistency_note": "Landmarks only, and they do hang together reasonably: all six landscape clips are daytime, dry, sun or light cloud, mostly static high-vantage or tripod shots, cool-season light (thin foliage, jackets). The three Almqvist clips (42 s) are one shoot; the 70 s Passeig de Gracia rooftop shot and La Pedrera match them well enough. The 18 s drone clip is a pre-cut montage and would need re-cutting. There is no train footage of any kind to be consistent with, so no journey look can be formed.",
 "sourcing_note": "Train footage for Barcelona: nothing found. Ten searches (metro, tram, subway/TMB, view from train window, Renfe/Rodalies, funicular/cable car/Tramvia Blau/Montjuic, Sants/Estacio de Franca, plus landmark queries) returned zero video pages showing a Barcelona metro, tram, Rodalies/Renfe train, funicular or cable car; the Renfe/Rodalies query returned no results at all, and the 'Barcelona metro' hits were photo listings. All 9 identifiable generic 'metro/train arriving' videos downloaded were other cities (Paris, New York x2, Liverpool, Warsaw, Netherlands, Edmonton, Dubai-like), 1 more was unidentifiable. Landmark/skyline clips titled 'Barcelona' are easy to find. Tool limit: fetch_pexels.sh resolved no id above ~21,000,000 (13 of 13 failed), so 2024+ uploads, including four Barcelona-titled street/landmark clips, are unmeasured; none of those unresolved pages is titled as a Barcelona train either. 18 downloads, all 18 viewed (work/audit/barcelona/sheet_1..3.jpg). Park Guell, Barceloneta, Gothic Quarter queries returned nothing specific. Steadiness/season judged from 4 stills per clip, not playback."
